# deident.tokens - SHIPPED EMPTY ON PURPOSE.
#
# One token per line. Blank lines and #-comments ignored. Matching is
# substring, case-insensitive by default (see --case-sensitive).
#
# DO NOT COMMIT REAL TOKENS TO THIS FILE.
# A committed token list is itself the leak: it is a tidy, greppable index of
# exactly the words someone did not want published. This file exists so the
# wiring is discoverable, not so it can be filled in.
#
# Keep your real list OUTSIDE the repository - a scratch directory, a secrets
# store, your CI secret - and point the scanner at it:
#
#     python tools/deident_scan.py --tokens <path-outside-the-repo> --strict
#
# What belongs on a real list (categories, not examples):
#   - every person's name, handle, and email local-part
#   - your organisation / client / product names that must not travel
#   - machine-specific absolute path fragments (user directory names, drive
#     letters plus a distinctive folder, sync-service folder names)
#   - internal repository, host, and project names
#   - session, ticket, and account identifiers
#
# Verify the scanner still fires before you trust a clean run:
#     python tools/deident_scan.py --selftest
